Theorem CH-1: Burden-registry-lattice composition soundness

  Preconditions:
    - BR is the burden-registry typed pre-pass output for function F
      (per-variable burden annotations consumed by the consumer per the
       sec-04A.2 design at docs/ori_lang/proposals/approved/aims-burden-tracking-proposal.md)
    - L is the lattice analysis converged AimsStateMap for F per IA-7
    - consume_stack(F, BR, L) is the sec-04A.2 elimination consumer:
      walks F's instruction stream; for each variable v with burden
      entries in BR, validates the elimination decision (DP-2 dec
      unnecessary OR DP-3 inc elidable) against L[v]'s converged
      lattice state
    - Lean 4 cross-validation MANDATORY per 00-overview.md MS-4
      critical-proof set (the Lean 4 cross-validation strategy)

  Soundness property:
    Forall v in vars(F).
      consume_stack(F, BR, L)[v] is consistent with L[v] under
      DP-2 (is_rc_dec_unnecessary) and DP-3 (is_rc_inc_elidable);
      no double-counting (burden writes do not race-invalidate
      elimination decisions);
      per-class coexistence well-formedness holds (lattice classes
      + burden classes do not overlap in their elimination claims).

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-11 coexistence handshake proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction
      interprocedural_summary
      case_analysis
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-11 discharges CH-1 composition proof

Theorem CH-2: DP-2 / DP-3 elimination consumer composition with predicate-stack-derived ops

  Preconditions:
    - DP-2 (is_rc_dec_unnecessary) and DP-3 (is_rc_inc_elidable) are
      pure-state predicates per Annex E §AIMS
    - Predicate-stack-derived ops are the sec-04A.2 burden-registry
      writes derived from active stack burden tracking
    - Coexistence claim: consume_stack reads BR + L; emits eliminations
      consistent with both — NO double-counting on stack consumers

  Soundness property:
    Forall v with burden(v) AND L[v].cardinality = absent.
      consume_stack emits exactly one elimination decision for v
      (not two — burden-derived AND lattice-derived emissions are
      THE SAME decision, not stacked).
      Equivalently: predicate-stack ops do NOT race-invalidate the
      lattice's DP-2 / DP-3 elimination claim.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-11 coexistence handshake proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction
      interprocedural_summary
      case_analysis
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-11 discharges CH-2 composition proof

Theorem CH-3: Per-class coexistence with active stack burden — three sub-classes

  Preconditions:
    - Three AIMS variable classes participate in burden coexistence:
        sub-class A: Owned x Linear x Once x Unique (RL-2 + RL-14 candidate)
        sub-class B: Borrowed x Linear x Once x Unique (RL-14 headerless candidate)
        sub-class C: MaybeShared x Many (RL-7 dynamic COW candidate)
    - Burden-registry annotations classify each variable into one of these
      three classes; coexistence requires per-class well-formedness

  Soundness property:
    Forall v in vars(F).
      class_of(v) = A: consume_stack honors RL-2 last-use dec AND RL-14
        stack-promotion field-level RcDec; burden annotation MUST agree.
      class_of(v) = B: consume_stack honors RL-14 headerless invariant;
        no RC emission; burden annotation MUST agree.
      class_of(v) = C: consume_stack honors RL-7 dynamic COW slow-path;
        burden annotation MUST flag MaybeShared.
      No variable in two classes; no variable without class assignment;
      coexistence well-formedness = total + disjoint class partition.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-11 coexistence handshake proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction
      interprocedural_summary
      case_analysis
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-11 discharges CH-3 composition proof

Theorem CH-4: AimsStateMap immutability under burden-registry mutation

  Preconditions:
    - L is the converged AimsStateMap for function F (output of IA-7)
    - BR is the burden-registry computed AFTER L's convergence per
      sec-04A.2 design (acyclic dependency: BR reads L, L does not
      depend on BR)
    - consume_stack walks the instruction stream with BOTH L (read-only)
      and BR (read-only) as inputs

  Soundness property:
    Forall mutation_event M of BR.
      L is NOT modified by M;
      L's per-variable AimsState values remain canonical (CN invariants
      preserved);
      L's per-block_entry_states + block_exit_states maps remain at
      their post-IA-7 converged values.
    Burden-registry mutations are SIDE-EFFECT-FREE w.r.t. AimsStateMap;
    no shared mutable state between BR computation and L computation.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-11 coexistence handshake proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction
      interprocedural_summary
      case_analysis
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-11 discharges CH-4 composition proof

Theorem CH-5: Phase-ordering composition — PL-1 interprocedural-first with burden-registry as Step 1 typed pre-pass

  Preconditions:
    - PL-1 mandates interprocedural-first ordering (Steps 1-2 across all
      functions before any per-function step) per Annex E §AIMS
    - Burden-registry pre-pass per sec-04A.2 design is a typed pre-pass
      input that lands on AimsStateMap (per arc.md sec-Non-Negotiable-Invariants
      invariant 5(c)) — NOT a new lattice dimension; NOT an independent
      RC emission path
    - Burden-registry runs as Step 1 typed pre-pass (BEFORE analyze_program)
      or as Step 4-companion pre-pass (BEFORE analyze_function), depending
      on per-variable vs per-function granularity

  Soundness property:
    Forall function F.
      pipeline order with burden-registry pre-pass inserted preserves
      PL-1 interprocedural-first invariant;
      burden-registry's BR(F) reads ONLY from F's call-graph predecessors'
      computed values (or F's own pre-pass values), NOT from F's
      not-yet-computed lattice values;
      PL-5 (no stale summaries) preserved: burden-registry pre-pass
      outputs become typed inputs to subsequent pipeline steps without
      circular dependency;
      PL-6 (adding-a-pass meta-rule) honored: pipeline ordering updated
      + constraint-no-violation proven.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-11 coexistence handshake proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction
      interprocedural_summary
      case_analysis
      lattice

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-11 discharges CH-5 composition proof
